ot found.\n\n**Debt (n5)**\n- **Spreads:** Caldrian utility bond spreads were 130bp in Q1 2026, 135bp in Q2 and 165bp in Q3. That is a 30bp widening in one quarter and 35bp above Q1.\n- **Access:** Norvane priced a C$1.1B bond \"comfortably\" in Q3, so investment-grade access is intact. This is the only confirmed debt deal. One deal does not show that Pellham can borrow at that scale.\n\n**Equity (n6)**\n- **Weak appetite:** Two utility share offerings were cut back in Q3. Pellham pulled its C$2.4B offering on 14 October. The source describes equity markets as \"less receptive\".\n\n**Pellham's response**\n- Pellham is the largest buyer of grid equipment in Caldria. It said it will cut 2027 transformer orders by about 40% and resize its Q1 2027 tender.\n- This suggests debt alone does not cover its plan at current costs, or that management does not want to add leverage.\n\n**Implication:** Expect 2027 capex to lean on debt, which is more expensive than before. Where a plan needed equity, expect it to be scaled back or deferred, as Pellham's was. For grid equipment demand, assume lower 2027 volume from Pellham rather than full funding of the plans.\n\n**Gaps:** I found no data on any of these:\n- all-in yields\n- total 2027 capex amounts\n- debt maturities\n- credit metrics such as ratings, FFO/debt or headroom\n- equity valuations, dilution or sector index performance\n\nI therefore can't say whether debt could fund the full plans.","ttft_ms":3466,"type":"result","duration_ms":52985,"uuid":"10851a30-8bc0-4b75-8847-614deed708d0","ttft_stream_ms":3240,"time_to_request_ms":70,"time_to_request_phases_ms":{"other":4,"system_prompt":8,"resume_other":0,"process_user_input":4,"input_attachments":13,"input_hooks":2,"conversation_append":1,"transcript_persist":2,"tool_pool_refresh":0,"init_message":6,"init_frame_send":1,"engine_pickup":1,"loop_entry":3,"message_prep":1,"model_config_wait":0,"autocompact":2,"request_announcements":6,"query_setup":0,"model_gates":0,"tool_schema